# Plannotation -- ignored files.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   uv.lock          CI runs `uv sync --locked` against it.
#   .python-version  Pins the contributor interpreter. CI sets UV_PYTHON from the
#                    matrix so this file never overrides a matrix cell.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so
*.pyd

# ------------------------------------------------------- build artefacts ----
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
MANIFEST

# ------------------------------------------------ uv / virtual environments --
.venv/
.venvs/
venv/
env/
.uv/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- tool caches ----
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pytest_cache/
.pytype/
.pyre/
.cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# -------------------------------------------------------------- coverage ----
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/
*.cover
nosetests.xml
junit*.xml
report.xml

# ----------------------------------------------------- secrets / local env --
# The benchmark harness reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the environment (a direnv
# .envrc, say) or from .env. No key ever belongs in the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.envrc.*
.pypirc
.netrc
*.pem
*.key

# ------------------------------------------------------------ real-world ----
# Inference is exercised against real construction PDFs -- third-party material
# that must NEVER be committed. The tests skip when the directory is absent,
# which is the state of every clean clone.
tests/fixtures/realworld/

# ------------------------------------------------ generated / heavy output --
# Vendored pdf.js build for the offline inspector: third-party and far over the
# 200 kB limit on committed binaries.
inspector/vendor/
# Cached model responses from the benchmark runner. bench/results/*.md and
# bench/questions.jsonl are committed; the response cache is not.
bench/.cache/
bench/cache/
# Documentation and GitHub Pages build output.
docs/_build/
site/
_site/

# Generated sample sets. `make samples` rebuilds them byte-identically from the
# models, so committing them would only let the drawings drift from the code that
# draws them. samples/README.md is written by hand and stays.
samples/*/
samples/groundtruth.jsonl

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ misc ----
*.log
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
